module

public import Silmaril.Proofs.Sim.X86.G.Method
public import Silmaril.Proofs.Sim.X86.G.Machine
public import Silmaril.Proofs.Sim.X86.G.VC
public import Silmaril.Proofs.Sim.X86.G.Jump

/-!
# The G simulator for x86-64: results

Definitions in `Silmaril.Sim.X86.G.Defs`; proofs in `Silmaril.Proofs.Sim.X86.G.*`. At every profile
and for every host relation, no axioms beyond `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`:

* **`emit_sound`** (per method): if the store encodes `σ` (`Enc`) and `Silmaril.X86.Ext.exec i σ`
  retires with `σ'`, the method's code evaluates to a store encoding `σ'`, changing only
  modelled globals; `core_sound` for the body without the RIP update; `emit_rip`.
* **`method_valid`**: every function instance running a method body meets `methodSpec`
  (`Silmaril.Wasm.Logic.Hoare.FSpecValid`): every call returns, ending in a store that encodes
  the x86 result of every state the initial store encodes. `simModule_*`: the methods of the
  quoted WAT module `simModule` are the generated bodies (`rfl`).
* `emitProg_sound`, `emitProg_twp`: translated straight-line programs terminate in every run in
  a store encoding the `runExt` result.
* **`hwp_transfer`** (old name `transfer`): an every-run (`HWP`) property of the translated program holds at a store
  encoding the x86 result; **`xproblem_of_wproblem`** (old name `reduce`): a `WProblem` (Wasm problem over the register globals)
  solves the corresponding `XProblem` (x86 problem on `runExt`).
* `run_of_runExt`: translated programs placed in memory (`CodeAt`, `BytesAt`) run on the
  `Silmaril.X86.Ext` machine (`stepOpt`) exactly as `runExt` says.
* `g_vc`: evaluates `wpc` on generated code (`hwp_of_wpc`).
-/

/-- info: 'Silmaril.Sim.X86.G.emit_sound' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] -/
